  "question": {
    "text": "A thin convex lens of focal length <math><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;is put on a plane mirror as shown in the figure. When an object is kept at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;from the lens-mirror combination, its image is formed at a distance <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> in front of the combination. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is:<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/beb6545b-56d2-48cc-a8c8-5fb1f2d2fbeb-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 136px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
